      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits on the Ohio River, making it Indiana’s easternmost settlement and a historic river‑town hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patriot%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Patriot’s downtown was largely rebuilt after a devastating fire in 1924 and a flood in 1937.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patriot%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Patriot Historical Society Museum preserves pioneer artifacts and steamboat relics that tell the town’s river‑town story.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://allthingsusa.blog/uncover-patriot-indiana-secrets-7-must-see-historical-gems",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Founded in the early 19th century, Patriot grew as part of a network of river communities that relied on the Ohio for trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
